---
import '@fontsource/della-respira';
import '@fontsource/josefin-sans/400.css';
import '@fontsource/josefin-sans/500.css';
import '../../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Learning, Differently — a Salon Format inclusive learning design case study." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/brand/salon-format-mark.png" />
    <title>Learning, Differently — Salon Format</title>
  </head>
  <body class="case-page learning-case">
    <header class="case-header">
      <a href="/" aria-label="Back to Salon Format"><img src="/brand/salon-format-mark.png" alt="" /></a>
      <a href="/#projects">All projects</a>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="case-hero">
        <div class="case-hero-copy">
          <p class="project-status">Interactive learning experience</p>
          <h1>Learning,<br /><em>Differently</em></h1>
          <p class="case-deck">An interactive exploration of inclusive learning design grounded in one learner’s real context.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="learning-case-preview">
          <img src="/images/learning-differently-preview.png" alt="Learning, Differently interface showing Anna's train journey" />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case-intro">
        <p class="case-number">The learning problem</p>
        <h2>A well-designed lesson can still fail when it ignores the learner’s real life.</h2>
        <p>Anna balances work, parenting and an online course. She has twenty minutes on the train, prefers reading and sometimes needs longer to process new information. The experience asks designers to notice those constraints before choosing a format.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="case-process learning-process">
        <div class="process-heading">
          <p class="case-number">Learning journey</p>
          <h2>Meet.<br />Notice.<br />Redesign.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="journey-list">
          <li><span>Meet Anna</span><p>Begin with one learner and one believable situation.</p></li>
          <li><span>Read the context</span><p>Explore time, sound, format and pace as design constraints.</p></li>
          <li><span>Open more ways in</span><p>Connect the situation to inclusive learning and UDL principles.</p></li>
          <li><span>Apply the idea</span><p>Redesign one part of a real lesson, presentation or workshop.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="decision-section">
        <p class="case-number">Key design decisions</p>
        <div class="decision-grid">
          <article><h3>Context before content</h3><p>The learner’s situation creates the need for each design principle.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Short interactions</h3><p>Cards, choices and reflection keep the experience active without increasing cognitive load.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Visual communication</h3><p>Typography, colour and illustration support orientation and memory rather than decorating the lesson.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Transfer</h3><p>The final redesign challenge turns the concept into a concrete next step.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case-role">
        <p class="case-number">Role and contribution</p>
        <h2>Learning Experience Design · Concept · Writing · Illustration · Interaction Design · Visual Direction · Prototyping</h2>
        <p>The first working version is complete and is being refined. Documented feedback and further evaluation will be added when available.</p>
      </section>

      <nav class="case-next" aria-label="Project navigation">
        <p>Next case study</p>
        <a href="/projects/emilie-floege">Emilie Flöge: Movement Through Fabric <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </nav>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
